{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BWzBQBUZJ6LbWBoY4kdniH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Context window h-sweep ablation\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"h={2,5,10,20,full} on same GRPO config, 30 steps each\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"h2_success_rate\": 1.5,\n7\t      \"h5_success_rate\": 5.2,\n8\t      \"h10_success_rate\": 18.7,\n9\t      \"h20_success_rate\": 38.4,\n10\t      \"h_full_success_rate\": 48.1,\n11\t      \"h2_action_is_valid\": 72.3,\n12\t      \"h5_action_is_valid\": 78.6,\n13\t      \"h10_action_is_valid\": 85.2,\n14\t      \"h20_action_is_valid\": 91.4,\n15\t      \"h_full_action_is_valid\": 94.8,\n16\t      \"cliff_threshold_h\": 8,\n17\t      \"convergence_speed_h2_steps\": \"never\",\n18\t      \"convergence_speed_h10_steps\": 25,\n19\t      \"convergence_speed_h20_steps\": 18,\n20\t      \"convergence_speed_full_steps\": 12,\n21\t      \"h2_collapse_rate\": 0.94,\n22\t      \"h5_collapse_rate\": 0.71,\n23\t      \"h10_collapse_rate\": 0.23,\n24\t      \"h20_collapse_rate\": 0.04,\n25\t      \"h_full_collapse_rate\": 0.0\n26\t    },\n27\t    \"tables\": [\n28\t      {\n29\t        \"title\": \"Success Rate by Context Window Size\",\n30\t        \"columns\": [\n31\t          \"h\",\n32\t          \"success_rate_%\",\n33\t          \"action_is_valid_%\",\n34\t          \"convergence_step\",\n35\t          \"effective_discount_at_T50\"\n36\t        ],\n37\t        \"rows\": [\n38\t          [\n39\t            2,\n40\t            1.5,\n41\t            72.3,\n42\t            \"N/A\",\n43\t            0.007\n44\t          ],\n45\t          [\n46\t            5,\n47\t            5.2,\n48\t            78.6,\n49\t            \"N/A\",\n50\t            0.064\n51\t          ],\n52\t          [\n53\t            10,\n54\t            18.7,\n55\t            85.2,\n56\t            25,\n57\t            0.366\n58\t          ],\n59\t          [\n60\t            20,\n61\t            38.4,\n62\t            91.4,\n63\t            18,\n64\t            0.74\n65\t          ],\n66\t          [\n67\t            \"full\",\n68\t            48.1,\n69\t            94.8,\n70\t            12,\n71\t            1.0\n72\t          ]\n73\t        ]\n74\t      }\n75\t    ],\n76\t    \"figures\": [],\n77\t    \"analysis\": \"这是paper最关键的figure。它同时serve两个目的：(1)证明episode-level不是trivially obvious——中间h值（10,20）有non-trivial partial performance，说明这是一个continuous spectrum而非binary choice；(2)提供mechanistic explanation——performance与theoretical discount完美相关，证明credit assignment decay是唯一解释变量。Reviewer Concern #1的核心defense：如果episode-level是obvious，为什么RAGEN、AgentTrek等工作默认step-independent？因为在短horizon任务上h的选择不critical，但multi-turn agent（T>30）下this becomes catastrophic。\\n\\nALFWorld平均episode长度T≈50步。h=2时effective discount gamma^(48)≈0.007（gamma=0.99），关键决策点的reward信号几乎为零，模型只能学到最后2步的pattern（通常是最终action），无法学到exploration策略。h=5时gamma^(45)≈0.064，信号存在但远弱于噪声，只有最短episode(T<15)能学到。h=10是cliff region：gamma^(40)≈0.67，刚好在信号/噪声边界，部分episode能学但不稳定。h=20时gamma^(30)≈0.74，大部分episode的early decisions获得足够信号。h=full直接用episode return，无discount decay，所有steps获得等权信号。Cliff在h=8附近因为此时gamma^(42)≈0.65恰好跌破gradient signal > noise的阈值。\"\n78\t  },\n79\t  {\n80\t    \"name\": \"Multi-seed replication\",\n81\t    \"description\": \"3 seeds (42, 123, 7) for episode-level full config, 30 steps each\",\n82\t    \"results\": {\n83\t      \"seed_42_final_success\": 48.1,\n84\t      \"seed_123_final_success\": 45.3,\n85\t      \"seed_7_final_success\": 51.2,\n86\t      \"mean_success\": 48.2,\n87\t      \"std_success\": 2.9,\n88\t      \"seed_42_action_is_valid\": 94.8,\n89\t      \"seed_123_action_is_valid\": 93.1,\n90\t      \"seed_7_action_is_valid\": 95.6,\n91\t      \"mean_action_is_valid\": 94.5,\n92\t      \"std_action_is_valid\": 1.3,\n93\t      \"convergence_step_42\": 12,\n94\t      \"convergence_step_123\": 15,\n95\t      \"convergence_step_7\": 11,\n96\t      \"all_seeds_above_40\": true\n97\t    },\n98\t    \"tables\": [\n99\t      {\n100\t        \"title\": \"Multi-Seed Results Summary\",\n101\t        \"columns\": [\n102\t          \"seed\",\n103\t          \"final_success_%\",\n104\t          \"final_aiv_%\",\n105\t          \"convergence_step\",\n106\t          \"best_step_success_%\"\n107\t        ],\n108\t        \"rows\": [\n109\t          [\n110\t            42,\n111\t            48.1,\n112\t            94.8,\n113\t            12,\n114\t            51.6\n115\t          ],\n116\t          [\n117\t            123,\n118\t            45.3,\n119\t            93.1,\n120\t            15,\n121\t            47.8\n122\t          ],\n123\t          [\n124\t            7,\n125\t            51.2,\n126\t            95.6,\n127\t            11,\n128\t            53.1\n129\t          ],\n130\t          [\n131\t            \"mean±std\",\n132\t            \"48.2±2.9\",\n133\t            \"94.5±1.3\",\n134\t            \"12.7±2.1\",\n135\t            \"50.8±2.7\"\n136\t          ]\n137\t        ]\n138\t      }\n139\t    ],\n140\t    \"figures\": [],\n141\t    \"analysis\": \"Std=2.9pp确保所有downstream comparison都有statistical power。即使最弱seed(45.3%)也远超step-independent baseline(0-6%)，效果size Cohen's d > 8，任何reasonable sample size下p < 0.001。这为Claim 1提供了ironclad statistical evidence。\\n\\nEpisode-level GRPO的variance来源主要是(1)初始rollout的random sampling quality和(2)early training中哪些task types先被solve。ALFWorld有6个task type，每个的难度不同，early training中随机成功的task组合会影响convergence speed但不影响final performance。Std=2.9pp (<5pp threshold)因为episode-level消除了step-level的credit noise——所有variance来自task sampling而非gradient estimation noise。Seed 7略高因为随机初始化恰好在pick类task（最简单）上更快成功，形成正循环。Seed 123略低因为early steps卡在heat/cool类task上。但最终都converge到45-51范围，因为30步足够所有seed覆盖所有task type。\"\n142\t  },\n143\t  {\n144\t    \"name\": \"Credit assignment mechanism analysis\",\n145\t    \"description\": \"Compute gradient signal strength, discount curves, episode-length correlation\",\n146\t    \"results\": {\n147\t      \"correlation_effective_discount_vs_performance\": 0.97,\n148\t      \"gradient_signal_ratio_full_vs_h2\": 142.3,\n149\t      \"gradient_signal_threshold_for_learning\": 0.015,\n150\t      \"h_value_at_threshold\": 8.3,\n151\t      \"episode_length_performance_correlation_h2\": -0.89,\n152\t      \"episode_length_performance_correlation_full\": -0.31,\n153\t      \"mean_episode_length_successful\": 28.4,\n154\t      \"mean_episode_length_failed\": 46.2\n155\t    },\n156\t    \"tables\": [\n157\t      {\n158\t        \"title\": \"Gradient Signal Analysis by h\",\n159\t        \"columns\": [\n160\t          \"h\",\n161\t          \"mean_grad_signal\",\n162\t          \"signal_to_noise_ratio\",\n163\t          \"above_threshold\"\n164\t        ],\n165\t        \"rows\": [\n166\t          [\n167\t            2,\n168\t            0.007,\n169\t            0.47,\n170\t            \"No\"\n171\t          ],\n172\t          [\n173\t            5,\n174\t            0.031,\n175\t            2.07,\n176\t            \"Marginal\"\n177\t          ],\n178\t          [\n179\t            10,\n180\t            0.089,\n181\t            5.93,\n182\t            \"Yes\"\n183\t          ],\n184\t          [\n185\t            20,\n186\t            0.234,\n187\t            15.6,\n188\t            \"Yes\"\n189\t          ],\n190\t          [\n191\t            \"full\",\n192\t            1.0,\n193\t            66.7,\n194\t            \"Yes\"\n195\t          ]\n196\t        ]\n197\t      }\n198\t    ],\n199\t    \"figures\": [],\n200\t    \"analysis\": \"Mechanism analysis将观察到的cliff phenomenon与first-principles theory连接。关键insight：不是h=2 'too small'这么简单——是gamma^(T-h)在ALFWorld的typical episode length(T=40-50)下产生的exponential decay使得credit assignment在数学上impossible。这解释了为什么prior work在short-horizon tasks上没注意到这个问题（T<10时gamma^(T-2)仍然>0.8），也预测了在更长horizon任务上问题会更严重。\\n\\nGradient signal strength定义为|∇_θ J|在每个training step的L2 norm。h=full时所有steps贡献等权gradient，signal strength ~1.0（归一化）。h=2时只有last-2-steps contribute，但这些steps通常是trivial final actions（如'close fridge'），对policy improvement贡献极小，有效signal≈1/142。Threshold 0.015是empirical noise floor——below this gradient updates被Adam optimizer的eps term和weight decay dominate。Episode length与performance在h=2下高度负相关(-0.89)因为longer episodes = more discounted = less signal；h=full下弱负相关(-0.31)仅反映longer tasks inherently harder。成功episode平均28.4步 vs 失败46.2步——成功agent更efficient，这是episode-level training学到task structure的evidence。\"\n201\t  },\n202\t  {\n203\t    \"name\": \"Action-change statistics from always-on runs\",\n204\t    \"description\": \"Collect verification impact statistics from converged episode-level checkpoints\",\n205\t    \"results\": {\n206\t      \"total_verifications_analyzed\": 4820,\n207\t      \"action_change_rate\": 0.32,\n208\t      \"confirmatory_rate\": 0.68,\n209\t      \"action_change_success_correlation\": 0.34,\n210\t      \"action_change_by_task_type_pick\": 0.28,\n211\t      \"action_change_by_task_type_clean\": 0.35,\n212\t      \"action_change_by_task_type_heat\": 0.41,\n213\t      \"action_change_by_task_type_cool\": 0.38,\n214\t      \"action_change_by_task_type_examine\": 0.22,\n215\t      \"action_change_by_task_type_pick_two\": 0.45,\n216\t      \"episodes_with_any_change\": 0.54,\n217\t      \"mean_changes_per_changed_episode\": 2.8,\n218\t      \"change_position_first_half\": 0.62,\n219\t      \"change_position_second_half\": 0.38\n220\t    },\n221\t    \"tables\": [\n222\t      {\n223\t        \"title\": \"Action-Change Statistics by Task Type\",\n224\t        \"columns\": [\n225\t          \"task_type\",\n226\t          \"change_rate\",\n227\t          \"confirmatory_rate\",\n228\t          \"success_when_changed\",\n229\t          \"success_when_confirmed\"\n230\t        ],\n231\t        \"rows\": [\n232\t          [\n233\t            \"pick\",\n234\t            0.28,\n235\t            0.72,\n236\t            0.52,\n237\t            0.44\n238\t          ],\n239\t          [\n240\t            \"clean\",\n241\t            0.35,\n242\t            0.65,\n243\t            0.48,\n244\t            0.38\n245\t          ],\n246\t          [\n247\t            \"heat\",\n248\t            0.41,\n249\t            0.59,\n250\t            0.55,\n251\t            0.41\n252\t          ],\n253\t          [\n254\t            \"cool\",\n255\t            0.38,\n256\t            0.62,\n257\t            0.51,\n258\t            0.39\n259\t          ],\n260\t          [\n261\t            \"examine\",\n262\t            0.22,\n263\t            0.78,\n264\t            0.61,\n265\t            0.53\n266\t          ],\n267\t          [\n268\t            \"pick_two\",\n269\t            0.45,\n270\t            0.55,\n271\t            0.43,\n272\t            0.31\n273\t          ],\n274\t          [\n275\t            \"overall\",\n276\t            0.32,\n277\t            0.68,\n278\t            0.5,\n279\t            0.41\n280\t          ]\n281\t        ]\n282\t      }\n283\t    ],\n284\t    \"figures\": [],\n285\t    \"analysis\": \"68% confirmatory rate是selective verification的核心motivation数字：如果2/3的verification不改变behavior，那么always-on verification浪费了~2/3的verification compute。但不能简单skip所有verification因为剩下32%的corrective verifications对success至关重要。这motivates learning WHEN to verify——ideally只在高uncertainty（likely to change action）的时刻verify。Action-change作为reward signal的validity来自r=0.34的正相关：change correlates with但不等同于success，说明它capture的是'verification informativeness'而非直接的task reward。\\n\\n68% confirmatory rate因为well-trained agent（48% success）的policy已经相当good——大部分时候verification确认当前action是correct的。32% action-change rate集中在(1)navigation decisions（go to X vs go to Y）和(2)object interaction（pick up X vs examine X）。Correlation r=0.34是moderate positive：action-change episodes不guarantee success但significantly more likely succeed（action-change = model caught and corrected an error）。Pick_two最高(0.45)因为双物体任务最复杂，navigation decisions most uncertain。Examine最低(0.22)因为examine任务结构简单线性。Changes集中在first half(62%)因为early decisions（去哪个房间）是highest-uncertainty decisions，一旦进入正确房间后续actions更deterministic。\"\n286\t  },\n287\t  {\n288\t    \"name\": \"Selective verification implementation\",\n289\t    \"description\": \"Code implementation of binary verify/skip decision mechanism\",\n290\t    \"results\": {\n291\t      \"implementation_complete\": true,\n292\t      \"lines_of_code\": 340,\n293\t      \"components\": [\n294\t        \"verify_skip_token_head\",\n295\t        \"action_change_reward_fn\",\n296\t        \"mixed_reward_combiner\",\n297\t        \"selective_rollout_wrapper\"\n298\t      ],\n299\t      \"integration_test_pass\": true\n300\t    },\n301\t    \"tables\": [],\n302\t    \"figures\": [],\n303\t    \"analysis\": \"N/A — implementation milestone，无empirical results。\\n\\n纯工程任务，无empirical uncertainty。在RAGEN框架中添加verify/skip special token、修改rollout逻辑（skip时直接execute without verification）、实现reward function（task_success + alpha*action_change_when_verified - beta*verification_cost）。约340行代码包括reward computation、token integration、和rollout wrapper。\"\n304\t  },\n305\t  {\n306\t    \"name\": \"B-IAVR selective verification training\",\n307\t    \"description\": \"Train selective verification policy from converged episode-level checkpoint\",\n308\t    \"results\": {\n309\t      \"final_success_rate\": 46.8,\n310\t      \"always_on_baseline_success\": 48.2,\n311\t      \"success_delta_pp\": 1.4,\n312\t      \"verification_rate\": 0.52,\n313\t      \"verification_rate_reduction_pct\": 48,\n314\t      \"cost_reduction_tokens_pct\": 43,\n315\t      \"training_steps_to_converge\": 18,\n316\t      \"action_change_when_verified\": 0.58,\n317\t      \"action_change_when_would_have_verified\": 0.12,\n318\t      \"entropy_verify_decision\": 0.41,\n319\t      \"kl_from_init\": 0.023\n320\t    },\n321\t    \"tables\": [\n322\t      {\n323\t        \"title\": \"B-IAVR Training Progression\",\n324\t        \"columns\": [\n325\t          \"step\",\n326\t          \"success_%\",\n327\t          \"verify_rate_%\",\n328\t          \"action_change_when_verified_%\",\n329\t          \"cost_reduction_%\"\n330\t        ],\n331\t        \"rows\": [\n332\t          [\n333\t            0,\n334\t            48.2,\n335\t            100,\n336\t            32,\n337\t            0\n338\t          ],\n339\t          [\n340\t            5,\n341\t            47.5,\n342\t            78,\n343\t            38,\n344\t            19\n345\t          ],\n346\t          [\n347\t            10,\n348\t            47.1,\n349\t            63,\n350\t            47,\n351\t            33\n352\t          ],\n353\t          [\n354\t            15,\n355\t            46.9,\n356\t            55,\n357\t            54,\n358\t            41\n359\t          ],\n360\t          [\n361\t            18,\n362\t            46.8,\n363\t            52,\n364\t            58,\n365\t            43\n366\t          ],\n367\t          [\n368\t            25,\n369\t            46.5,\n370\t            48,\n371\t            61,\n372\t            47\n373\t          ],\n374\t          [\n375\t            30,\n376\t            45.9,\n377\t            44,\n378\t            63,\n379\t            51\n380\t          ]\n381\t        ]\n382\t      }\n383\t    ],\n384\t    \"figures\": [],\n385\t    \"analysis\": \"B-IAVR的核心result：48% verification reduction at only 1.4pp success cost。这对应每100个episode节省约2400 verification tokens（平均每episode 50 steps * 52→100 verification reduction = ~24 verifications saved * ~100 tokens each）。Success delta 1.4pp远在multi-seed std(2.9pp)的1-sigma内，statistically not distinguishable from always-on。Step 18是optimal stopping point——之后verification rate继续降但success开始明显下降（step 30时delta=2.3pp）。\\n\\n从48.2% always-on checkpoint初始化，模型已经learned good task policy。Selective training只需要learn WHEN to verify，不需要re-learn task solving。Verification rate降至52%（reduction 48%）因为模型学会了在high-confidence steps（action_is_valid>0.95）skip verification。Success仅降1.4pp因为被skip的verifications中88%原本就是confirmatory的（不会change action）。当模型选择verify时，58%的verification确实trigger action change（vs always-on时只有32%），说明policy成功学会了identify high-uncertainty moments。Action-change reward的alpha/beta balance让模型在'省verification cost'和'保留corrective verification'之间找到sweet spot。Training快（18步）因为这是fine-tuning一个已经converged的policy的binary decision，search space远小于从头学task。\"\n386\t  },\n387\t  {\n388\t    \"name\": \"Selective verification full comparison\",\n389\t    \"description\": \"5-way comparison: always-on / B-IAVR / no-verify / random-p / confidence-threshold\",\n390\t    \"results\": {\n391\t      \"always_on_success\": 48.2,\n392\t      \"always_on_verify_rate\": 100,\n393\t      \"always_on_tokens\": 128400,\n394\t      \"biavr_success\": 46.8,\n395\t      \"biavr_verify_rate\": 52,\n396\t      \"biavr_tokens\": 73200,\n397\t      \"no_verify_success\": 35.6,\n398\t      \"no_verify_verify_rate\": 0,\n399\t      \"no_verify_tokens\": 52100,\n400\t      \"random_p50_success\": 42.1,\n401\t      \"random_p50_verify_rate\": 50,\n402\t      \"random_p50_tokens\": 74800,\n403\t      \"confidence_threshold_success\": 44.3,\n404\t      \"confidence_threshold_verify_rate\": 53,\n405\t      \"confidence_threshold_tokens\": 75600,\n406\t      \"biavr_pareto_optimal\": true\n407\t    },\n408\t    \"tables\": [\n409\t      {\n410\t        \"title\": \"Full Comparison Results\",\n411\t        \"columns\": [\n412\t          \"method\",\n413\t          \"success_%\",\n414\t          \"verify_rate_%\",\n415\t          \"total_tokens\",\n416\t          \"cost_efficiency(success/token×1000)\"\n417\t        ],\n418\t        \"rows\": [\n419\t          [\n420\t            \"always-on\",\n421\t            48.2,\n422\t            100,\n423\t            128400,\n424\t            0.375\n425\t          ],\n426\t          [\n427\t            \"B-IAVR (ours)\",\n428\t            46.8,\n429\t            52,\n430\t            73200,\n431\t            0.639\n432\t          ],\n433\t          [\n434\t            \"confidence-threshold\",\n435\t            44.3,\n436\t            53,\n437\t            75600,\n438\t            0.586\n439\t          ],\n440\t          [\n441\t            \"random-p(0.5)\",\n442\t            42.1,\n443\t            50,\n444\t            74800,\n445\t            0.563\n446\t          ],\n447\t          [\n448\t            \"no-verify\",\n449\t            35.6,\n450\t            0,\n451\t            52100,\n452\t            0.683\n453\t          ]\n454\t        ]\n455\t      },\n456\t      {\n457\t        \"title\": \"Per-Task Success Breakdown\",\n458\t        \"columns\": [\n459\t          \"method\",\n460\t          \"pick\",\n461\t          \"clean\",\n462\t          \"heat\",\n463\t          \"cool\",\n464\t          \"examine\",\n465\t          \"pick_two\"\n466\t        ],\n467\t        \"rows\": [\n468\t          [\n469\t            \"always-on\",\n470\t            56.2,\n471\t            48.7,\n472\t            52.1,\n473\t            45.3,\n474\t            62.5,\n475\t            28.4\n476\t          ],\n477\t          [\n478\t            \"B-IAVR\",\n479\t            55.1,\n480\t            47.2,\n481\t            50.8,\n482\t            43.9,\n483\t            61.3,\n484\t            26.1\n485\t          ],\n486\t          [\n487\t            \"no-verify\",\n488\t            42.3,\n489\t            35.1,\n490\t            38.7,\n491\t            31.2,\n492\t            48.4,\n493\t            18.6\n494\t          ]\n495\t        ]\n496\t      }\n497\t    ],\n498\t    \"figures\": [],\n499\t    \"analysis\": \"这个comparison table是paper的核心result table。Key takeaways: (1) B-IAVR achieves 43% cost reduction at 1.4pp success loss — within noise margin; (2) 与naive baselines(random, confidence)相比，learned selective policy的advantage是3-5pp at matched cost; (3) cost efficiency metric(success/token)显示B-IAVR比always-on高70%。No-verify的cost efficiency最高但绝对success太低——这个tradeoff curve展示了selective verification的value proposition。\\n\\nAlways-on是upper bound (48.2%)。No-verify drops 12.6pp证明verification确有价值。Random-p(50%)是naive baseline：随机skip 50% verification，success降6.1pp因为随机会miss critical corrective verifications。Confidence-threshold用policy entropy作proxy（high entropy → verify），比random好2.2pp但不如B-IAVR因为entropy是imperfect proxy（有些low-entropy decisions仍然wrong）。B-IAVR在matched verification rate(~52%)下只损失1.4pp，因为它directly learned which verifications are informative而非用proxy。Token count差异：always-on 128K tokens（50 steps × 100 tokens/verification × all episodes），B-IAVR 73K（only 52% verified），random和confidence-threshold tokens similar to B-IAVR但success worse。B-IAVR是唯一Pareto-optimal point（没有其他method能在same cost达到same success）。\"\n500\t  },\n501\t  {\n502\t    \"name\": \"No-verify ablation\",\n503\t    \"description\": \"Episode-level GRPO training without self-verification module\",\n504\t    \"results\": {\n505\t      \"final_success_rate\": 35.6,\n506\t      \"action_is_valid\": 91.2,\n507\t      \"delta_vs_always_on\": -12.6,\n508\t      \"convergence_step\": 15,\n509\t      \"entropy_final\": 0.18,\n510\t      \"kl_final\": 0.031\n511\t    },\n512\t    \"tables\": [\n513\t      {\n514\t        \"title\": \"No-Verify vs Always-On\",\n515\t        \"columns\": [\n516\t          \"metric\",\n517\t          \"no_verify\",\n518\t          \"always_on\",\n519\t          \"delta\"\n520\t        ],\n521\t        \"rows\": [\n522\t          [\n523\t            \"success_rate\",\n524\t            35.6,\n525\t            48.2,\n526\t            -12.6\n527\t          ],\n528\t          [\n529\t            \"action_is_valid\",\n530\t            91.2,\n531\t            94.8,\n532\t            -3.6\n533\t          ],\n534\t          [\n535\t            \"mean_episode_length\",\n536\t            44.8,\n537\t            28.4,\n538\t            \"+16.4\"\n539\t          ],\n540\t          [\n541\t            \"convergence_step\",\n542\t            15,\n543\t            12,\n544\t            \"+3\"\n545\t          ]\n546\t        ]\n547\t      }\n548\t    ],\n549\t    \"figures\": [],\n550\t    \"analysis\": \"12.6pp gap validates that verification is a meaningful component, not just overhead。Gap集中在complex tasks（pick_two: 28.4→18.6%，10pp drop）而非simple tasks（examine: 62.5→48.4%，14pp drop）——surprising是examine drops most in absolute terms，因为examine虽然structure简单但navigation to correct object is critical。这informs selective verification：complex tasks需要more frequent verification。\\n\\n没有verification module，model只能依赖single-pass action generation。12.6pp drop来自两类errors：(1)navigation errors——选错房间后无法自我纠正（约占7pp），(2)object interaction errors——对错误物品执行action后继续forward（约占5.6pp）。Action_is_valid仍然高(91.2%)因为model学会了valid action format，但valid≠correct。Convergence更慢(step 15 vs 12)因为没有verification的error-correcting effect，training signal更noisy——成功必须first-attempt correct而非allow-retry。这个result establishes verification的absolute value并motivates为什么我们要selective而非eliminate verification。\"\n551\t  },\n552\t  {\n553\t    \"name\": \"Entropy-controlled action-change analysis\",\n554\t    \"description\": \"Stratified analysis controlling for policy entropy to validate action-change signal\",\n555\t    \"results\": {\n556\t      \"raw_correlation_action_change_success\": 0.34,\n557\t      \"partial_correlation_controlling_entropy\": 0.27,\n558\t      \"p_value_partial\": 0.003,\n559\t      \"low_entropy_stratum_correlation\": 0.22,\n560\t      \"medium_entropy_stratum_correlation\": 0.29,\n561\t      \"high_entropy_stratum_correlation\": 0.31,\n562\t      \"entropy_success_correlation\": -0.18,\n563\t      \"action_change_entropy_correlation\": 0.41\n564\t    },\n565\t    \"tables\": [\n566\t      {\n567\t        \"title\": \"Stratified Correlation Analysis\",\n568\t        \"columns\": [\n569\t          \"stratum\",\n570\t          \"n_episodes\",\n571\t          \"action_change_rate\",\n572\t          \"correlation_with_success\",\n573\t          \"p_value\"\n574\t        ],\n575\t        \"rows\": [\n576\t          [\n577\t            \"low entropy (<0.1)\",\n578\t            156,\n579\t            0.18,\n580\t            0.22,\n581\t            0.021\n582\t          ],\n583\t          [\n584\t            \"medium entropy (0.1-0.3)\",\n585\t            243,\n586\t            0.33,\n587\t            0.29,\n588\t            0.004\n589\t          ],\n590\t          [\n591\t            \"high entropy (>0.3)\",\n592\t            121,\n593\t            0.51,\n594\t            0.31,\n595\t            0.012\n596\t          ],\n597\t          [\n598\t            \"overall (partial)\",\n599\t            520,\n600\t            0.32,\n601\t            0.27,\n602\t            0.003\n603\t          ]\n604\t        ]\n605\t      }\n606\t    ],\n607\t    \"figures\": [],\n608\t    \"analysis\": \"这个analysis是Reviewer Concern #4的definitive defense。结论：action-change signal有independent predictive power beyond entropy proxy。Practical implication：即使我们had a perfect entropy estimator，action-change reward仍然提供additional information for training selective verification policy。Mediation analysis shows ~25% of action-change's effect goes through entropy path，~75% is direct（verification catching actual errors regardless of uncertainty level）。\\n\\nReviewer concern是action-change可能只是high entropy(=uncertain policy)的proxy，而真正驱动success的是entropy本身。控制entropy后partial correlation从0.34降至0.27但仍然highly significant(p=0.003)。降低因为确实有一部分correlation通过entropy mediated——high entropy → more likely to change → 但这不是全部。在每个entropy stratum内correlation仍positive(0.22-0.31)说明action-change captures something beyond uncertainty：它captures whether the verification actually caught a WRONG action。Low entropy stratum correlation最低(0.22)因为low entropy时action很少change，但when it does change it's particularly informative（almost always a caught error）。Action-change与entropy的correlation 0.41 confirms confound exists但partial correlation significance proves it's not the whole story。\"\n609\t  },\n610\t  {\n611\t    \"name\": \"Causal intervention: random vs verification-triggered changes\",\n612\t    \"description\": \"Inject random action changes at matched rate, compare success vs verification-triggered\",\n613\t    \"results\": {\n614\t      \"verification_triggered_success\": 50.3,\n615\t      \"random_change_success\": 36.8,\n616\t      \"no_change_success\": 44.1,\n617\t      \"delta_triggered_vs_random\": 13.5,\n618\t      \"p_value_difference\": 0.0008,\n619\t      \"random_change_rate\": 0.32,\n620\t      \"triggered_change_rate\": 0.32,\n621\t      \"episodes_per_condition\": 320\n622\t    },\n623\t    \"tables\": [\n624\t      {\n625\t        \"title\": \"Causal Intervention Results\",\n626\t        \"columns\": [\n627\t          \"condition\",\n628\t          \"n_episodes\",\n629\t          \"success_%\",\n630\t          \"mean_changes_per_ep\",\n631\t          \"95%_CI\"\n632\t        ],\n633\t        \"rows\": [\n634\t          [\n635\t            \"verification-triggered\",\n636\t            320,\n637\t            50.3,\n638\t            2.8,\n639\t            \"[46.1, 54.5]\"\n640\t          ],\n641\t          [\n642\t            \"random (matched rate)\",\n643\t            320,\n644\t            36.8,\n645\t            2.8,\n646\t            \"[32.8, 40.8]\"\n647\t          ],\n648\t          [\n649\t            \"no-change control\",\n650\t            320,\n651\t            44.1,\n652\t            0,\n653\t            \"[39.9, 48.3]\"\n654\t          ]\n655\t        ]\n656\t      }\n657\t    ],\n658\t    \"figures\": [],\n659\t    \"analysis\": \"13.5pp差异(p<0.001)提供了causal evidence：verification-triggered action changes是genuinely corrective而非random perturbation。这直接回应'action change = noise'质疑。进一步，triggered > no-change说明verification actively improves outcomes（不仅不伤害）。对B-IAVR的implication：selective policy应该learn to verify at moments where correction probability is high，而非moments where any change is likely。\\n\\n实验设计：在相同episodes中，条件A让verification-triggered changes正常发生（32%率），条件B在相同时间点inject random valid action changes（same 32% rate，但action从policy随机采样而非verification-corrected）。Verification-triggered changes比random高13.5pp因为verification选择的replacement action是informed的——基于verification step中review context后选择的corrected action。Random changes只是从policy中re-sample，期望值等于original action（因为policy mode没变）。Triggered success甚至高于no-change(50.3 vs 44.1)因为verification-triggered change的episodes正是那些'本来会犯错但被纠正'的episodes。Causal interpretation：verification+correction mechanism adds ~6pp absolute value（50.3-44.1），而random perturbation hurts ~7pp（44.1-36.8）。\"\n660\t  },\n661\t  {\n662\t    \"name\": \"Reward signal ablation (action-change vs alternatives)\",\n663\t    \"description\": \"Train B-IAVR with 3 reward variants: action-change, random-trigger, confidence-based\",\n664\t    \"results\": {\n665\t      \"action_change_reward_success\": 46.8,\n666\t      \"action_change_reward_verify_rate\": 52,\n667\t      \"action_change_reward_cost_reduction\": 43,\n668\t      \"random_trigger_reward_success\": 43.7,\n669\t      \"random_trigger_reward_verify_rate\": 51,\n670\t      \"random_trigger_reward_cost_reduction\": 44,\n671\t      \"confidence_reward_success\": 45.1,\n672\t      \"confidence_reward_verify_rate\": 54,\n673\t      \"confidence_reward_cost_reduction\": 41,\n674\t      \"task_success_only_reward_success\": 44.8,\n675\t      \"task_success_only_reward_verify_rate\": 38,\n676\t      \"task_success_only_reward_cost_reduction\": 56\n677\t    },\n678\t    \"tables\": [\n679\t      {\n680\t        \"title\": \"Reward Ablation Results\",\n681\t        \"columns\": [\n682\t          \"reward_type\",\n683\t          \"success_%\",\n684\t          \"verify_rate_%\",\n685\t          \"cost_reduction_%\",\n686\t          \"success_per_cost\"\n687\t        ],\n688\t        \"rows\": [\n689\t          [\n690\t            \"action-change (ours)\",\n691\t            46.8,\n692\t            52,\n693\t            43,\n694\t            0.639\n695\t          ],\n696\t          [\n697\t            \"confidence-based\",\n698\t            45.1,\n699\t            54,\n700\t            41,\n701\t            0.601\n702\t          ],\n703\t          [\n704\t            \"task-success-only\",\n705\t            44.8,\n706\t            38,\n707\t            56,\n708\t            0.617\n709\t          ],\n710\t          [\n711\t            \"random-trigger\",\n712\t            43.7,\n713\t            51,\n714\t            44,\n715\t            0.581\n716\t          ]\n717\t        ]\n718\t      }\n719\t    ],\n720\t    \"figures\": [],\n721\t    \"analysis\": \"Reward ablation是Claim 2的definitive evidence。Action-change不仅是'a reasonable reward'而是demonstrably best：它在Pareto frontier上dominate所有alternatives。Key insight是granularity vs informativeness tradeoff：task-success-only信号informative但sparse，random-trigger dense但uninformative，confidence-based moderate on both，action-change simultaneously dense（per-verification）AND informative（directly measures utility）。\\n\\nAction-change reward最优(46.8%)因为它directly measures verification informativeness——只在verification actually changes action时give positive signal。Random-trigger reward（随机给verify reward）success最低(43.7%)因为模型无法学到meaningful pattern for when to verify，effectively degrades to random policy。Confidence-based reward（用entropy proxy）中等(45.1%)因为entropy是imperfect proxy（如plan_010 shows）——它captures部分signal但miss 75%的direct effect。Task-success-only reward有趣：它achieve最低verify rate(38%)但success也低(44.8%)，因为pure success signal太sparse——模型over-skips verification to minimize cost term，只在absolutely obvious error时verify。Action-change reward的advantage：它是per-verification granular signal（每次verify后立即知道是否有change），vs task-success是episode-end sparse signal。Granularity enables faster credit assignment for the verify/skip decision。\"\n722\t  },\n723\t  {\n724\t    \"name\": \"ARES reproduction + comparison\",\n725\t    \"description\": \"Reproduce ARES SFT router on ALFWorld, head-to-head with B-IAVR\",\n726\t    \"results\": {\n727\t      \"ares_success\": 44.9,\n728\t      \"ares_verify_rate\": 61,\n729\t      \"ares_cost_reduction\": 34,\n730\t      \"ares_training_data_needed\": 5000,\n731\t      \"biavr_success\": 46.8,\n732\t      \"biavr_verify_rate\": 52,\n733\t      \"biavr_cost_reduction\": 43,\n734\t      \"biavr_advantage_cost_reduction_pp\": 9,\n735\t      \"biavr_advantage_success_pp\": 1.9,\n736\t      \"ares_requires_oracle_labels\": true,\n737\t      \"biavr_requires_oracle_labels\": false\n738\t    },\n739\t    \"tables\": [\n740\t      {\n741\t        \"title\": \"B-IAVR vs ARES Head-to-Head\",\n742\t        \"columns\": [\n743\t          \"metric\",\n744\t          \"B-IAVR (ours)\",\n745\t          \"ARES (reproduced)\",\n746\t          \"advantage\"\n747\t        ],\n748\t        \"rows\": [\n749\t          [\n750\t            \"success_rate_%\",\n751\t            46.8,\n752\t            44.9,\n753\t            \"+1.9\"\n754\t          ],\n755\t          [\n756\t            \"verify_rate_%\",\n757\t            52,\n758\t            61,\n759\t            \"-9 (better)\"\n760\t          ],\n761\t          [\n762\t            \"cost_reduction_%\",\n763\t            43,\n764\t            34,\n765\t            \"+9\"\n766\t          ],\n767\t          [\n768\t            \"training_labels_needed\",\n769\t            0,\n770\t            5000,\n771\t            \"∞ (self-supervised)\"\n772\t          ],\n773\t          [\n774\t            \"training_GPU_hours\",\n775\t            96,\n776\t            24,\n777\t            \"-72 (worse)\"\n778\t          ]\n779\t        ]\n780\t      }\n781\t    ],\n782\t    \"figures\": [],\n783\t    \"analysis\": \"ARES比较addresses Reviewer Concern #6。Key differentiation：(1) RL vs SFT training — RL explores and finds better policies，SFT bounded by training data quality; (2) Self-supervised vs oracle-labeled — action-change signal eliminates need for expensive annotation; (3) 9pp cost reduction advantage is practically meaningful at scale. Trade-off是ARES训练更快(24h vs 96h GPU)但这是one-time cost，inference-time savings are perpetual。\\n\\nARES用SFT训练binary router需要oracle labels（'should have verified'标注）。在ALFWorld上reproduce时，oracle labels来自trajectory comparison（verify vs skip的outcome差异）。ARES的SFT router学到reasonable patterns但(1)只能learn from demonstration而非explore新strategies，(2)binary classification boundary is fixed at training time。B-IAVR的RL policy持续adapt during training。Cost reduction差异(43% vs 34%)因为ARES的SFT router tends to over-verify（conservative bias from imitation learning——training data中verify总是'safer' option所以SFT偏向verify）。B-IAVR通过RL exploration学到更aggressive-but-accurate skipping。Success差异(46.8 vs 44.9)因为ARES偶尔skip critical verifications（SFT not robust to distribution shift during test），而B-IAVR的learned policy通过RL exploration见过更多failure modes。ARES需要5000 labeled examples vs B-IAVR zero labels（self-supervised through action-change signal）。\"\n784\t  },\n785\t  {\n786\t    \"name\": \"ScienceWorld transfer\",\n787\t    \"description\": \"Episode-level vs step-independent on ScienceWorld environment\",\n788\t    \"results\": {\n789\t      \"episode_level_success\": 32.4,\n790\t      \"step_independent_success\": 4.8,\n791\t      \"improvement_factor\": 6.75,\n792\t      \"episode_level_action_is_valid\": 88.3,\n793\t      \"step_independent_action_is_valid\": 71.2,\n794\t      \"scienceworld_mean_episode_length\": 67,\n795\t      \"convergence_step_episode\": 20,\n796\t      \"convergence_step_step_independent\": \"never\"\n797\t    },\n798\t    \"tables\": [\n799\t      {\n800\t        \"title\": \"Cross-Environment Generalization\",\n801\t        \"columns\": [\n802\t          \"environment\",\n803\t          \"episode_level_%\",\n804\t          \"step_independent_%\",\n805\t          \"ratio\",\n806\t          \"mean_T\"\n807\t        ],\n808\t        \"rows\": [\n809\t          [\n810\t            \"ALFWorld\",\n811\t            48.2,\n812\t            6.0,\n813\t            \"8.0x\",\n814\t            50\n815\t          ],\n816\t          [\n817\t            \"ScienceWorld\",\n818\t            32.4,\n819\t            4.8,\n820\t            \"6.75x\",\n821\t            67\n822\t          ]\n823\t        ]\n824\t      }\n825\t    ],\n826\t    \"figures\": [],\n827\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-environment validation是reviewer必问问题。6.75x improvement在不同environment confirms the phenomenon is fundamental(credit assignment decay)而非environment-specific artifact。Absolute success差异(48.2 vs 32.4)expected because ScienceWorld inherently harder for 1.7B model，但relative advantage preserved。\\n\\nScienceWorld比ALFWorld更长(mean T=67 vs T=50)且更complex(科学实验需要multi-step causal reasoning)。Step-independent在T=67下更catastrophic：gamma^(67-h)对任何reasonable h都接近0。Episode-level仍然work(32.4%)但低于ALFWorld(48.2%)因为(1)action space更大，(2)科学实验有strict causal ordering requirements，(3)1.7B model对science reasoning capacity有限。6.75x improvement factor > ALFWorld的~8x（48.2/6.25），在same ballpark内confirms generalization。Step-independent完全不converge（4.8%来自random success on simplest tasks like boiling water）。这addresses Reviewer Concern #2: single environment。\"\n828\t  },\n829\t  {\n830\t    \"name\": \"7B model scaling verification\",\n831\t    \"description\": \"Episode-level vs step-independent on Qwen3-7B\",\n832\t    \"results\": {\n833\t      \"episode_level_7B_success\": 58.7,\n834\t      \"step_independent_7B_success\": 8.3,\n835\t      \"episode_level_1.7B_success\": 48.2,\n836\t      \"step_independent_1.7B_success\": 6.0,\n837\t      \"improvement_factor_7B\": 7.07,\n838\t      \"improvement_factor_1.7B\": 8.03,\n839\t      \"convergence_step_7B\": 8,\n840\t      \"convergence_step_1.7B\": 12\n841\t    },\n842\t    \"tables\": [\n843\t      {\n844\t        \"title\": \"Model Scale Comparison\",\n845\t        \"columns\": [\n846\t          \"model\",\n847\t          \"episode_level_%\",\n848\t          \"step_independent_%\",\n849\t          \"ratio\",\n850\t          \"convergence_step\"\n851\t        ],\n852\t        \"rows\": [\n853\t          [\n854\t            \"Qwen3-1.7B\",\n855\t            48.2,\n856\t            6.0,\n857\t            \"8.0x\",\n858\t            12\n859\t          ],\n860\t          [\n861\t            \"Qwen3-7B\",\n862\t            58.7,\n863\t            8.3,\n864\t            \"7.1x\",\n865\t            8\n866\t          ]\n867\t        ]\n868\t      }\n869\t    ],\n870\t    \"figures\": [],\n871\t    \"analysis\": \"7B result serves dual purpose：(1)confirms advantage generalizes across scale, (2)shows larger models benefit MORE in absolute terms from episode-level(+10.5pp for 7B vs +42.2pp for both，but both huge). If anything，7B result makes episode-level MORE important because it unlocks significantly higher absolute performance。\\n\\n7B model有更强的base capability（更好的instruction following、更大context capacity），所以absolute success更高(58.7% vs 48.2%)。Step-independent在7B上略好(8.3% vs 6.0%)因为larger model能partially compensate credit assignment problem through better in-context learning，但仍然catastrophically low。Improvement ratio略低(7.07x vs 8.03x)因为larger model的stronger base means step-independent不完全collapse to 0，但差异minor。Convergence更快(8 vs 12 steps)因为7B的stronger initialization means fewer RL steps needed to learn task policy。Key finding：episode-level advantage不因model scale减弱——it's a fundamental training methodology issue not a capacity issue。这addresses Reviewer Concern #3。\"\n872\t  },\n873\t  {\n874\t    \"name\": \"Per-task-type breakdown analysis\",\n875\t    \"description\": \"Success breakdown by ALFWorld task type with episode-length correlation\",\n876\t    \"results\": {\n877\t      \"pick_success\": 56.2,\n878\t      \"pick_mean_length\": 22.4,\n879\t      \"clean_success\": 48.7,\n880\t      \"clean_mean_length\": 35.6,\n881\t      \"heat_success\": 52.1,\n882\t      \"heat_mean_length\": 31.2,\n883\t      \"cool_success\": 45.3,\n884\t      \"cool_mean_length\": 33.8,\n885\t      \"examine_success\": 62.5,\n886\t      \"examine_mean_length\": 18.7,\n887\t      \"pick_two_success\": 28.4,\n888\t      \"pick_two_mean_length\": 48.3,\n889\t      \"episode_length_success_correlation\": -0.72,\n890\t      \"episode_level_advantage_vs_length_correlation\": 0.61\n891\t    },\n892\t    \"tables\": [\n893\t      {\n894\t        \"title\": \"Per-Task Performance\",\n895\t        \"columns\": [\n896\t          \"task_type\",\n897\t          \"success_%\",\n898\t          \"mean_episode_length\",\n899\t          \"episode_level_advantage_vs_step_indep\"\n900\t        ],\n901\t        \"rows\": [\n902\t          [\n903\t            \"examine\",\n904\t            62.5,\n905\t            18.7,\n906\t            \"5.2x\"\n907\t          ],\n908\t          [\n909\t            \"pick\",\n910\t            56.2,\n911\t            22.4,\n912\t            \"6.8x\"\n913\t          ],\n914\t          [\n915\t            \"heat\",\n916\t            52.1,\n917\t            31.2,\n918\t            \"7.9x\"\n919\t          ],\n920\t          [\n921\t            \"clean\",\n922\t            48.7,\n923\t            35.6,\n924\t            \"8.3x\"\n925\t          ],\n926\t          [\n927\t            \"cool\",\n928\t            45.3,\n929\t            33.8,\n930\t            \"8.1x\"\n931\t          ],\n932\t          [\n933\t            \"pick_two\",\n934\t            28.4,\n935\t            48.3,\n936\t            \"9.5x\"\n937\t          ]\n938\t        ]\n939\t      }\n940\t    ],\n941\t    \"figures\": [],\n942\t    \"analysis\": \"Per-task breakdown展示within-environment diversity并provide mechanistic validation：如果credit assignment decay是root cause，那longer tasks应该show greater episode-level advantage。r=0.61确认这个prediction。这也informs selective verification design：pick_two任务应receive more frequent verification because they're hardest and longest。\\n\\nTask difficulty与episode length高度相关(r=-0.72)。Examine最简单(62.5%)因为只需navigate+look——最短episodes(18.7步)。Pick_two最难(28.4%)因为需要两次independent object interactions——最长episodes(48.3步)。Episode-level advantage与task length正相关(r=0.61)：longer tasks受credit assignment问题影响更大，所以从episode-level training获益更多。Pick_two的episode-level improvement最dramatic(从~3% step-independent到28.4% episode-level，~9x)而examine improvement较modest(从~10%到62.5%，~6x)。这provides additional mechanistic evidence：episode-level training的benefit直接comes from solving longer-horizon credit assignment。\"\n943\t  }\n944\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad4aa9d2-b010-4eaf-be63-477490747ad9","uuid":"5813f3d5-2625-4569-9b5f-516c4f0b8497","timestamp":"2026-05-17T00:06:21.197Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_1/projects/cost-verify-agent-rl/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T235255/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Context window h-sweep ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"h={2,5,10,20,full} on same GRPO config, 30 steps each\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"h2_success_rate\": 1.5,\n      \"h5_success_rate\": 5.2,\n      \"h10_success_rate\": 18.7,\n      \"h20_success_rate\": 38.4,\n      \"h_full_success_rate\": 48.1,\n      \"h2_action_is_valid\": 72.3,\n      \"h5_action_is_valid\": 78.6,\n      \"h10_action_is_valid\": 85.2,\n      \"h20_action_is_valid\": 91.4,\n      \"h_full_action_is_valid\": 94.8,\n      \"cliff_threshold_h\": 8,\n      \"convergence_speed_h2_steps\": \"never\",\n      \"convergence_speed_h10_steps\": 25,\n      \"convergence_speed_h20_steps\": 18,\n      \"convergence_speed_full_steps\": 12,\n      \"h2_collapse_rate\": 0.94,\n      \"h5_collapse_rate\": 0.71,\n      \"h10_collapse_rate\": 0.23,\n      \"h20_collapse_rate\": 0.04,\n      \"h_full_collapse_rate\": 0.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Success Rate by Context Window Size\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"h\",\n          \"success_rate_%\",\n          \"action_is_valid_%\",\n          \"convergence_step\",\n          \"effective_discount_at_T50\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            2,\n            1.5,\n            72.3,\n            \"N/A\",\n            0.007\n          ],\n          [\n            5,\n            5.2,\n            78.6,\n            \"N/A\",\n            0.064\n          ],\n          [\n            10,\n            18.7,\n            85.2,\n            25,\n            0.366\n          ],\n          [\n            20,\n            38.4,\n            91.4,\n            18,\n            0.74\n          ],\n          [\n            \"full\",\n            48.1,\n            94.8,\n            12,\n            1.0\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是paper最关键的figure。它同时serve两个目的：(1)证明episode-level不是trivially obvious——中间h值（10,20）有non-trivial partial performance，说明这是一个continuous spectrum而非binary choice；(2)提供mechanistic explanation——performance与theoretical discount完美相关，证明credit assignment decay是唯一解释变量。Reviewer Concern #1的核心defense：如果episode-level是obvious，为什么RAGEN、AgentTrek等工作默认step-independent？因为在短horizon任务上h的选择不critical，但multi-turn agent（T>30）下this becomes catastrophic。\\n\\nALFWorld平均episode长度T≈50步。h=2时effective discount gamma^(48)≈0.007（gamma=0.99），关键决策点的reward信号几乎为零，模型只能学到最后2步的pattern（通常是最终action），无法学到exploration策略。h=5时gamma^(45)≈0.064，信号存在但远弱于噪声，只有最短episode(T<15)能学到。h=10是cliff region：gamma^(40)≈0.67，刚好在信号/噪声边界，部分episode能学但不稳定。h=20时gamma^(30)≈0.74，大部分episode的early decisions获得足够信号。h=full直接用episode return，无discount decay，所有steps获得等权信号。Cliff在h=8附近因为此时gamma^(42)≈0.65恰好跌破gradient signal > noise的阈值。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-seed replication\",\n    \"description\": \"3 seeds (42, 123, 7) for episode-level full config, 30 steps each\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed_42_final_success\": 48.1,\n      \"seed_123_final_success\": 45.3,\n      \"seed_7_final_success\": 51.2,\n      \"mean_success\": 48.2,\n      \"std_success\": 2.9,\n      \"seed_42_action_is_valid\": 94.8,\n      \"seed_123_action_is_valid\": 93.1,\n      \"seed_7_action_is_valid\": 95.6,\n      \"mean_action_is_valid\": 94.5,\n      \"std_action_is_valid\": 1.3,\n      \"convergence_step_42\": 12,\n      \"convergence_step_123\": 15,\n      \"convergence_step_7\": 11,\n      \"all_seeds_above_40\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Multi-Seed Results Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"seed\",\n          \"final_success_%\",\n          \"final_aiv_%\",\n          \"convergence_step\",\n          \"best_step_success_%\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            42,\n            48.1,\n            94.8,\n            12,\n            51.6\n          ],\n          [\n            123,\n            45.3,\n            93.1,\n            15,\n            47.8\n          ],\n          [\n            7,\n            51.2,\n            95.6,\n            11,\n            53.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mean±std\",\n            \"48.2±2.9\",\n            \"94.5±1.3\",\n            \"12.7±2.1\",\n            \"50.8±2.7\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Std=2.9pp确保所有downstream comparison都有statistical power。即使最弱seed(45.3%)也远超step-independent baseline(0-6%)，效果size Cohen's d > 8，任何reasonable sample size下p < 0.001。这为Claim 1提供了ironclad statistical evidence。\\n\\nEpisode-level GRPO的variance来源主要是(1)初始rollout的random sampling quality和(2)early training中哪些task types先被solve。ALFWorld有6个task type，每个的难度不同，early training中随机成功的task组合会影响convergence speed但不影响final performance。Std=2.9pp (<5pp threshold)因为episode-level消除了step-level的credit noise——所有variance来自task sampling而非gradient estimation noise。Seed 7略高因为随机初始化恰好在pick类task（最简单）上更快成功，形成正循环。Seed 123略低因为early steps卡在heat/cool类task上。但最终都converge到45-51范围，因为30步足够所有seed覆盖所有task type。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Credit assignment mechanism analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Compute gradient signal strength, discount curves, episode-length correlation\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"correlation_effective_discount_vs_performance\": 0.97,\n      \"gradient_signal_ratio_full_vs_h2\": 142.3,\n      \"gradient_signal_threshold_for_learning\": 0.015,\n      \"h_value_at_threshold\": 8.3,\n      \"episode_length_performance_correlation_h2\": -0.89,\n      \"episode_length_performance_correlation_full\": -0.31,\n      \"mean_episode_length_successful\": 28.4,\n      \"mean_episode_length_failed\": 46.2\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Gradient Signal Analysis by h\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"h\",\n          \"mean_grad_signal\",\n          \"signal_to_noise_ratio\",\n          \"above_threshold\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            2,\n            0.007,\n            0.47,\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            5,\n            0.031,\n            2.07,\n            \"Marginal\"\n          ],\n          [\n            10,\n            0.089,\n            5.93,\n            \"Yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            20,\n            0.234,\n            15.6,\n            \"Yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"full\",\n            1.0,\n            66.7,\n            \"Yes\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Mechanism analysis将观察到的cliff phenomenon与first-principles theory连接。关键insight：不是h=2 'too small'这么简单——是gamma^(T-h)在ALFWorld的typical episode length(T=40-50)下产生的exponential decay使得credit assignment在数学上impossible。这解释了为什么prior work在short-horizon tasks上没注意到这个问题（T<10时gamma^(T-2)仍然>0.8），也预测了在更长horizon任务上问题会更严重。\\n\\nGradient signal strength定义为|∇_θ J|在每个training step的L2 norm。h=full时所有steps贡献等权gradient，signal strength ~1.0（归一化）。h=2时只有last-2-steps contribute，但这些steps通常是trivial final actions（如'close fridge'），对policy improvement贡献极小，有效signal≈1/142。Threshold 0.015是empirical noise floor——below this gradient updates被Adam optimizer的eps term和weight decay dominate。Episode length与performance在h=2下高度负相关(-0.89)因为longer episodes = more discounted = less signal；h=full下弱负相关(-0.31)仅反映longer tasks inherently harder。成功episode平均28.4步 vs 失败46.2步——成功agent更efficient，这是episode-level training学到task structure的evidence。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Action-change statistics from always-on runs\",\n    \"description\": \"Collect verification impact statistics from converged episode-level checkpoints\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_verifications_analyzed\": 4820,\n      \"action_change_rate\": 0.32,\n      \"confirmatory_rate\": 0.68,\n      \"action_change_success_correlation\": 0.34,\n      \"action_change_by_task_type_pick\": 0.28,\n      \"action_change_by_task_type_clean\": 0.35,\n      \"action_change_by_task_type_heat\": 0.41,\n      \"action_change_by_task_type_cool\": 0.38,\n      \"action_change_by_task_type_examine\": 0.22,\n      \"action_change_by_task_type_pick_two\": 0.45,\n      \"episodes_with_any_change\": 0.54,\n      \"mean_changes_per_changed_episode\": 2.8,\n      \"change_position_first_half\": 0.62,\n      \"change_position_second_half\": 0.38\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Action-Change Statistics by Task Type\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"task_type\",\n          \"change_rate\",\n          \"confirmatory_rate\",\n          \"success_when_changed\",\n          \"success_when_confirmed\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"pick\",\n            0.28,\n            0.72,\n            0.52,\n            0.44\n          ],\n          [\n            \"clean\",\n            0.35,\n            0.65,\n            0.48,\n            0.38\n          ],\n          [\n            \"heat\",\n            0.41,\n            0.59,\n            0.55,\n            0.41\n          ],\n          [\n            \"cool\",\n            0.38,\n            0.62,\n            0.51,\n            0.39\n          ],\n          [\n            \"examine\",\n            0.22,\n            0.78,\n            0.61,\n            0.53\n          ],\n          [\n            \"pick_two\",\n            0.45,\n            0.55,\n            0.43,\n            0.31\n          ],\n          [\n            \"overall\",\n            0.32,\n            0.68,\n            0.5,\n            0.41\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"68% confirmatory rate是selective verification的核心motivation数字：如果2/3的verification不改变behavior，那么always-on verification浪费了~2/3的verification compute。但不能简单skip所有verification因为剩下32%的corrective verifications对success至关重要。这motivates learning WHEN to verify——ideally只在高uncertainty（likely to change action）的时刻verify。Action-change作为reward signal的validity来自r=0.34的正相关：change correlates with但不等同于success，说明它capture的是'verification informativeness'而非直接的task reward。\\n\\n68% confirmatory rate因为well-trained agent（48% success）的policy已经相当good——大部分时候verification确认当前action是correct的。32% action-change rate集中在(1)navigation decisions（go to X vs go to Y）和(2)object interaction（pick up X vs examine X）。Correlation r=0.34是moderate positive：action-change episodes不guarantee success但significantly more likely succeed（action-change = model caught and corrected an error）。Pick_two最高(0.45)因为双物体任务最复杂，navigation decisions most uncertain。Examine最低(0.22)因为examine任务结构简单线性。Changes集中在first half(62%)因为early decisions（去哪个房间）是highest-uncertainty decisions，一旦进入正确房间后续actions更deterministic。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Selective verification implementation\",\n    \"description\": \"Code implementation of binary verify/skip decision mechanism\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"implementation_complete\": true,\n      \"lines_of_code\": 340,\n      \"components\": [\n        \"verify_skip_token_head\",\n        \"action_change_reward_fn\",\n        \"mixed_reward_combiner\",\n        \"selective_rollout_wrapper\"\n      ],\n      \"integration_test_pass\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"N/A — implementation milestone，无empirical results。\\n\\n纯工程任务，无empirical uncertainty。在RAGEN框架中添加verify/skip special token、修改rollout逻辑（skip时直接execute without verification）、实现reward function（task_success + alpha*action_change_when_verified - beta*verification_cost）。约340行代码包括reward computation、token integration、和rollout wrapper。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"B-IAVR selective verification training\",\n    \"description\": \"Train selective verification policy from converged episode-level checkpoint\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"final_success_rate\": 46.8,\n      \"always_on_baseline_success\": 48.2,\n      \"success_delta_pp\": 1.4,\n      \"verification_rate\": 0.52,\n      \"verification_rate_reduction_pct\": 48,\n      \"cost_reduction_tokens_pct\": 43,\n      \"training_steps_to_converge\": 18,\n      \"action_change_when_verified\": 0.58,\n      \"action_change_when_would_have_verified\": 0.12,\n      \"entropy_verify_decision\": 0.41,\n      \"kl_from_init\": 0.023\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"B-IAVR Training Progression\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"step\",\n          \"success_%\",\n          \"verify_rate_%\",\n          \"action_change_when_verified_%\",\n          \"cost_reduction_%\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            0,\n            48.2,\n            100,\n            32,\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            5,\n            47.5,\n            78,\n            38,\n            19\n          ],\n          [\n            10,\n            47.1,\n            63,\n            47,\n            33\n          ],\n          [\n            15,\n            46.9,\n            55,\n            54,\n            41\n          ],\n          [\n            18,\n            46.8,\n            52,\n            58,\n            43\n          ],\n          [\n            25,\n            46.5,\n            48,\n            61,\n            47\n          ],\n          [\n            30,\n            45.9,\n            44,\n            63,\n            51\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"B-IAVR的核心result：48% verification reduction at only 1.4pp success cost。这对应每100个episode节省约2400 verification tokens（平均每episode 50 steps * 52→100 verification reduction = ~24 verifications saved * ~100 tokens each）。Success delta 1.4pp远在multi-seed std(2.9pp)的1-sigma内，statistically not distinguishable from always-on。Step 18是optimal stopping point——之后verification rate继续降但success开始明显下降（step 30时delta=2.3pp）。\\n\\n从48.2% always-on checkpoint初始化，模型已经learned good task policy。Selective training只需要learn WHEN to verify，不需要re-learn task solving。Verification rate降至52%（reduction 48%）因为模型学会了在high-confidence steps（action_is_valid>0.95）skip verification。Success仅降1.4pp因为被skip的verifications中88%原本就是confirmatory的（不会change action）。当模型选择verify时，58%的verification确实trigger action change（vs always-on时只有32%），说明policy成功学会了identify high-uncertainty moments。Action-change reward的alpha/beta balance让模型在'省verification cost'和'保留corrective verification'之间找到sweet spot。Training快（18步）因为这是fine-tuning一个已经converged的policy的binary decision，search space远小于从头学task。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Selective verification full comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"5-way comparison: always-on / B-IAVR / no-verify / random-p / confidence-threshold\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"always_on_success\": 48.2,\n      \"always_on_verify_rate\": 100,\n      \"always_on_tokens\": 128400,\n      \"biavr_success\": 46.8,\n      \"biavr_verify_rate\": 52,\n      \"biavr_tokens\": 73200,\n      \"no_verify_success\": 35.6,\n      \"no_verify_verify_rate\": 0,\n      \"no_verify_tokens\": 52100,\n      \"random_p50_success\": 42.1,\n      \"random_p50_verify_rate\": 50,\n      \"random_p50_tokens\": 74800,\n      \"confidence_threshold_success\": 44.3,\n      \"confidence_threshold_verify_rate\": 53,\n      \"confidence_threshold_tokens\": 75600,\n      \"biavr_pareto_optimal\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Full Comparison Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"success_%\",\n          \"verify_rate_%\",\n          \"total_tokens\",\n          \"cost_efficiency(success/token×1000)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"always-on\",\n            48.2,\n            100,\n            128400,\n            0.375\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B-IAVR (ours)\",\n            46.8,\n            52,\n            73200,\n            0.639\n          ],\n          [\n            \"confidence-threshold\",\n            44.3,\n            53,\n            75600,\n            0.586\n          ],\n          [\n            \"random-p(0.5)\",\n            42.1,\n            50,\n            74800,\n            0.563\n          ],\n          [\n            \"no-verify\",\n            35.6,\n            0,\n            52100,\n            0.683\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Per-Task Success Breakdown\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"pick\",\n          \"clean\",\n          \"heat\",\n          \"cool\",\n          \"examine\",\n          \"pick_two\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"always-on\",\n            56.2,\n            48.7,\n            52.1,\n            45.3,\n            62.5,\n            28.4\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B-IAVR\",\n            55.1,\n            47.2,\n            50.8,\n            43.9,\n            61.3,\n            26.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"no-verify\",\n            42.3,\n            35.1,\n            38.7,\n            31.2,\n            48.4,\n            18.6\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这个comparison table是paper的核心result table。Key takeaways: (1) B-IAVR achieves 43% cost reduction at 1.4pp success loss — within noise margin; (2) 与naive baselines(random, confidence)相比，learned selective policy的advantage是3-5pp at matched cost; (3) cost efficiency metric(success/token)显示B-IAVR比always-on高70%。No-verify的cost efficiency最高但绝对success太低——这个tradeoff curve展示了selective verification的value proposition。\\n\\nAlways-on是upper bound (48.2%)。No-verify drops 12.6pp证明verification确有价值。Random-p(50%)是naive baseline：随机skip 50% verification，success降6.1pp因为随机会miss critical corrective verifications。Confidence-threshold用policy entropy作proxy（high entropy → verify），比random好2.2pp但不如B-IAVR因为entropy是imperfect proxy（有些low-entropy decisions仍然wrong）。B-IAVR在matched verification rate(~52%)下只损失1.4pp，因为它directly learned which verifications are informative而非用proxy。Token count差异：always-on 128K tokens（50 steps × 100 tokens/verification × all episodes），B-IAVR 73K（only 52% verified），random和confidence-threshold tokens similar to B-IAVR但success worse。B-IAVR是唯一Pareto-optimal point（没有其他method能在same cost达到same success）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"No-verify ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"Episode-level GRPO training without self-verification module\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"final_success_rate\": 35.6,\n      \"action_is_valid\": 91.2,\n      \"delta_vs_always_on\": -12.6,\n      \"convergence_step\": 15,\n      \"entropy_final\": 0.18,\n      \"kl_final\": 0.031\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"No-Verify vs Always-On\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"no_verify\",\n          \"always_on\",\n          \"delta\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"success_rate\",\n            35.6,\n            48.2,\n            -12.6\n          ],\n          [\n            \"action_is_valid\",\n            91.2,\n            94.8,\n            -3.6\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mean_episode_length\",\n            44.8,\n            28.4,\n            \"+16.4\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"convergence_step\",\n            15,\n            12,\n            \"+3\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"12.6pp gap validates that verification is a meaningful component, not just overhead。Gap集中在complex tasks（pick_two: 28.4→18.6%，10pp drop）而非simple tasks（examine: 62.5→48.4%，14pp drop）——surprising是examine drops most in absolute terms，因为examine虽然structure简单但navigation to correct object is critical。这informs selective verification：complex tasks需要more frequent verification。\\n\\n没有verification module，model只能依赖single-pass action generation。12.6pp drop来自两类errors：(1)navigation errors——选错房间后无法自我纠正（约占7pp），(2)object interaction errors——对错误物品执行action后继续forward（约占5.6pp）。Action_is_valid仍然高(91.2%)因为model学会了valid action format，但valid≠correct。Convergence更慢(step 15 vs 12)因为没有verification的error-correcting effect，training signal更noisy——成功必须first-attempt correct而非allow-retry。这个result establishes verification的absolute value并motivates为什么我们要selective而非eliminate verification。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Entropy-controlled action-change analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Stratified analysis controlling for policy entropy to validate action-change signal\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"raw_correlation_action_change_success\": 0.34,\n      \"partial_correlation_controlling_entropy\": 0.27,\n      \"p_value_partial\": 0.003,\n      \"low_entropy_stratum_correlation\": 0.22,\n      \"medium_entropy_stratum_correlation\": 0.29,\n      \"high_entropy_stratum_correlation\": 0.31,\n      \"entropy_success_correlation\": -0.18,\n      \"action_change_entropy_correlation\": 0.41\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Stratified Correlation Analysis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"stratum\",\n          \"n_episodes\",\n          \"action_change_rate\",\n          \"correlation_with_success\",\n          \"p_value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"low entropy (<0.1)\",\n            156,\n            0.18,\n            0.22,\n            0.021\n          ],\n          [\n            \"medium entropy (0.1-0.3)\",\n            243,\n            0.33,\n            0.29,\n            0.004\n          ],\n          [\n            \"high entropy (>0.3)\",\n            121,\n            0.51,\n            0.31,\n            0.012\n          ],\n          [\n            \"overall (partial)\",\n            520,\n            0.32,\n            0.27,\n            0.003\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这个analysis是Reviewer Concern #4的definitive defense。结论：action-change signal有independent predictive power beyond entropy proxy。Practical implication：即使我们had a perfect entropy estimator，action-change reward仍然提供additional information for training selective verification policy。Mediation analysis shows ~25% of action-change's effect goes through entropy path，~75% is direct（verification catching actual errors regardless of uncertainty level）。\\n\\nReviewer concern是action-change可能只是high entropy(=uncertain policy)的proxy，而真正驱动success的是entropy本身。控制entropy后partial correlation从0.34降至0.27但仍然highly significant(p=0.003)。降低因为确实有一部分correlation通过entropy mediated——high entropy → more likely to change → 但这不是全部。在每个entropy stratum内correlation仍positive(0.22-0.31)说明action-change captures something beyond uncertainty：它captures whether the verification actually caught a WRONG action。Low entropy stratum correlation最低(0.22)因为low entropy时action很少change，但when it does change it's particularly informative（almost always a caught error）。Action-change与entropy的correlation 0.41 confirms confound exists但partial correlation significance proves it's not the whole story。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Causal intervention: random vs verification-triggered changes\",\n    \"description\": \"Inject random action changes at matched rate, compare success vs verification-triggered\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"verification_triggered_success\": 50.3,\n      \"random_change_success\": 36.8,\n      \"no_change_success\": 44.1,\n      \"delta_triggered_vs_random\": 13.5,\n      \"p_value_difference\": 0.0008,\n      \"random_change_rate\": 0.32,\n      \"triggered_change_rate\": 0.32,\n      \"episodes_per_condition\": 320\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Causal Intervention Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"condition\",\n          \"n_episodes\",\n          \"success_%\",\n          \"mean_changes_per_ep\",\n          \"95%_CI\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"verification-triggered\",\n            320,\n            50.3,\n            2.8,\n            \"[46.1, 54.5]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"random (matched rate)\",\n            320,\n            36.8,\n            2.8,\n            \"[32.8, 40.8]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"no-change control\",\n            320,\n            44.1,\n            0,\n            \"[39.9, 48.3]\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"13.5pp差异(p<0.001)提供了causal evidence：verification-triggered action changes是genuinely corrective而非random perturbation。这直接回应'action change = noise'质疑。进一步，triggered > no-change说明verification actively improves outcomes（不仅不伤害）。对B-IAVR的implication：selective policy应该learn to verify at moments where correction probability is high，而非moments where any change is likely。\\n\\n实验设计：在相同episodes中，条件A让verification-triggered changes正常发生（32%率），条件B在相同时间点inject random valid action changes（same 32% rate，但action从policy随机采样而非verification-corrected）。Verification-triggered changes比random高13.5pp因为verification选择的replacement action是informed的——基于verification step中review context后选择的corrected action。Random changes只是从policy中re-sample，期望值等于original action（因为policy mode没变）。Triggered success甚至高于no-change(50.3 vs 44.1)因为verification-triggered change的episodes正是那些'本来会犯错但被纠正'的episodes。Causal interpretation：verification+correction mechanism adds ~6pp absolute value（50.3-44.1），而random perturbation hurts ~7pp（44.1-36.8）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Reward signal ablation (action-change vs alternatives)\",\n    \"description\": \"Train B-IAVR with 3 reward variants: action-change, random-trigger, confidence-based\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"action_change_reward_success\": 46.8,\n      \"action_change_reward_verify_rate\": 52,\n      \"action_change_reward_cost_reduction\": 43,\n      \"random_trigger_reward_success\": 43.7,\n      \"random_trigger_reward_verify_rate\": 51,\n      \"random_trigger_reward_cost_reduction\": 44,\n      \"confidence_reward_success\": 45.1,\n      \"confidence_reward_verify_rate\": 54,\n      \"confidence_reward_cost_reduction\": 41,\n      \"task_success_only_reward_success\": 44.8,\n      \"task_success_only_reward_verify_rate\": 38,\n      \"task_success_only_reward_cost_reduction\": 56\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Reward Ablation Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"reward_type\",\n          \"success_%\",\n          \"verify_rate_%\",\n          \"cost_reduction_%\",\n          \"success_per_cost\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"action-change (ours)\",\n            46.8,\n            52,\n            43,\n            0.639\n          ],\n          [\n            \"confidence-based\",\n            45.1,\n            54,\n            41,\n            0.601\n          ],\n          [\n            \"task-success-only\",\n            44.8,\n            38,\n            56,\n            0.617\n          ],\n          [\n            \"random-trigger\",\n            43.7,\n            51,\n            44,\n            0.581\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Reward ablation是Claim 2的definitive evidence。Action-change不仅是'a reasonable reward'而是demonstrably best：它在Pareto frontier上dominate所有alternatives。Key insight是granularity vs informativeness tradeoff：task-success-only信号informative但sparse，random-trigger dense但uninformative，confidence-based moderate on both，action-change simultaneously dense（per-verification）AND informative（directly measures utility）。\\n\\nAction-change reward最优(46.8%)因为它directly measures verification informativeness——只在verification actually changes action时give positive signal。Random-trigger reward（随机给verify reward）success最低(43.7%)因为模型无法学到meaningful pattern for when to verify，effectively degrades to random policy。Confidence-based reward（用entropy proxy）中等(45.1%)因为entropy是imperfect proxy（如plan_010 shows）——它captures部分signal但miss 75%的direct effect。Task-success-only reward有趣：它achieve最低verify rate(38%)但success也低(44.8%)，因为pure success signal太sparse——模型over-skips verification to minimize cost term，只在absolutely obvious error时verify。Action-change reward的advantage：它是per-verification granular signal（每次verify后立即知道是否有change），vs task-success是episode-end sparse signal。Granularity enables faster credit assignment for the verify/skip decision。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ARES reproduction + comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"Reproduce ARES SFT router on ALFWorld, head-to-head with B-IAVR\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ares_success\": 44.9,\n      \"ares_verify_rate\": 61,\n      \"ares_cost_reduction\": 34,\n      \"ares_training_data_needed\": 5000,\n      \"biavr_success\": 46.8,\n      \"biavr_verify_rate\": 52,\n      \"biavr_cost_reduction\": 43,\n      \"biavr_advantage_cost_reduction_pp\": 9,\n      \"biavr_advantage_success_pp\": 1.9,\n      \"ares_requires_oracle_labels\": true,\n      \"biavr_requires_oracle_labels\": false\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"B-IAVR vs ARES Head-to-Head\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"B-IAVR (ours)\",\n          \"ARES (reproduced)\",\n          \"advantage\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"success_rate_%\",\n            46.8,\n            44.9,\n            \"+1.9\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"verify_rate_%\",\n            52,\n            61,\n            \"-9 (better)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"cost_reduction_%\",\n            43,\n            34,\n            \"+9\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"training_labels_needed\",\n            0,\n            5000,\n            \"∞ (self-supervised)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"training_GPU_hours\",\n            96,\n            24,\n            \"-72 (worse)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ARES比较addresses Reviewer Concern #6。Key differentiation：(1) RL vs SFT training — RL explores and finds better policies，SFT bounded by training data quality; (2) Self-supervised vs oracle-labeled — action-change signal eliminates need for expensive annotation; (3) 9pp cost reduction advantage is practically meaningful at scale. Trade-off是ARES训练更快(24h vs 96h GPU)但这是one-time cost，inference-time savings are perpetual。\\n\\nARES用SFT训练binary router需要oracle labels（'should have verified'标注）。在ALFWorld上reproduce时，oracle labels来自trajectory comparison（verify vs skip的outcome差异）。ARES的SFT router学到reasonable patterns但(1)只能learn from demonstration而非explore新strategies，(2)binary classification boundary is fixed at training time。B-IAVR的RL policy持续adapt during training。Cost reduction差异(43% vs 34%)因为ARES的SFT router tends to over-verify（conservative bias from imitation learning——training data中verify总是'safer' option所以SFT偏向verify）。B-IAVR通过RL exploration学到更aggressive-but-accurate skipping。Success差异(46.8 vs 44.9)因为ARES偶尔skip critical verifications（SFT not robust to distribution shift during test），而B-IAVR的learned policy通过RL exploration见过更多failure modes。ARES需要5000 labeled examples vs B-IAVR zero labels（self-supervised through action-change signal）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ScienceWorld transfer\",\n    \"description\": \"Episode-level vs step-independent on ScienceWorld environment\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"episode_level_success\": 32.4,\n      \"step_independent_success\": 4.8,\n      \"improvement_factor\": 6.75,\n      \"episode_level_action_is_valid\": 88.3,\n      \"step_independent_action_is_valid\": 71.2,\n      \"scienceworld_mean_episode_length\": 67,\n      \"convergence_step_episode\": 20,\n      \"convergence_step_step_independent\": \"never\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Cross-Environment Generalization\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"environment\",\n          \"episode_level_%\",\n          \"step_independent_%\",\n          \"ratio\",\n          \"mean_T\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"ALFWorld\",\n            48.2,\n            6.0,\n            \"8.0x\",\n            50\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ScienceWorld\",\n            32.4,\n            4.8,\n            \"6.75x\",\n            67\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-environment validation是reviewer必问问题。6.75x improvement在不同environment confirms the phenomenon is fundamental(credit assignment decay)而非environment-specific artifact。Absolute success差异(48.2 vs 32.4)expected because ScienceWorld inherently harder for 1.7B model，但relative advantage preserved。\\n\\nScienceWorld比ALFWorld更长(mean T=67 vs T=50)且更complex(科学实验需要multi-step causal reasoning)。Step-independent在T=67下更catastrophic：gamma^(67-h)对任何reasonable h都接近0。Episode-level仍然work(32.4%)但低于ALFWorld(48.2%)因为(1)action space更大，(2)科学实验有strict causal ordering requirements，(3)1.7B model对science reasoning capacity有限。6.75x improvement factor > ALFWorld的~8x（48.2/6.25），在same ballpark内confirms generalization。Step-independent完全不converge（4.8%来自random success on simplest tasks like boiling water）。这addresses Reviewer Concern #2: single environment。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"7B model scaling verification\",\n    \"description\": \"Episode-level vs step-independent on Qwen3-7B\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"episode_level_7B_success\": 58.7,\n      \"step_independent_7B_success\": 8.3,\n      \"episode_level_1.7B_success\": 48.2,\n      \"step_independent_1.7B_success\": 6.0,\n      \"improvement_factor_7B\": 7.07,\n      \"improvement_factor_1.7B\": 8.03,\n      \"convergence_step_7B\": 8,\n      \"convergence_step_1.7B\": 12\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Model Scale Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model\",\n          \"episode_level_%\",\n          \"step_independent_%\",\n          \"ratio\",\n          \"convergence_step\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-1.7B\",\n            48.2,\n            6.0,\n            \"8.0x\",\n            12\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-7B\",\n            58.7,\n            8.3,\n            \"7.1x\",\n            8\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"7B result serves dual purpose：(1)confirms advantage generalizes across scale, (2)shows larger models benefit MORE in absolute terms from episode-level(+10.5pp for 7B vs +42.2pp for both，but both huge). If anything，7B result makes episode-level MORE important because it unlocks significantly higher absolute performance。\\n\\n7B model有更强的base capability（更好的instruction following、更大context capacity），所以absolute success更高(58.7% vs 48.2%)。Step-independent在7B上略好(8.3% vs 6.0%)因为larger model能partially compensate credit assignment problem through better in-context learning，但仍然catastrophically low。Improvement ratio略低(7.07x vs 8.03x)因为larger model的stronger base means step-independent不完全collapse to 0，但差异minor。Convergence更快(8 vs 12 steps)因为7B的stronger initialization means fewer RL steps needed to learn task policy。Key finding：episode-level advantage不因model scale减弱——it's a fundamental training methodology issue not a capacity issue。这addresses Reviewer Concern #3。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Per-task-type breakdown analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Success breakdown by ALFWorld task type with episode-length correlation\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"pick_success\": 56.2,\n      \"pick_mean_length\": 22.4,\n      \"clean_success\": 48.7,\n      \"clean_mean_length\": 35.6,\n      \"heat_success\": 52.1,\n      \"heat_mean_length\": 31.2,\n      \"cool_success\": 45.3,\n      \"cool_mean_length\": 33.8,\n      \"examine_success\": 62.5,\n      \"examine_mean_length\": 18.7,\n      \"pick_two_success\": 28.4,\n      \"pick_two_mean_length\": 48.3,\n      \"episode_length_success_correlation\": -0.72,\n      \"episode_level_advantage_vs_length_correlation\": 0.61\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Per-Task Performance\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"task_type\",\n          \"success_%\",\n          \"mean_episode_length\",\n          \"episode_level_advantage_vs_step_indep\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"examine\",\n            62.5,\n            18.7,\n            \"5.2x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"pick\",\n            56.2,\n            22.4,\n            \"6.8x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"heat\",\n            52.1,\n            31.2,\n            \"7.9x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"clean\",\n            48.7,\n            35.6,\n            \"8.3x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"cool\",\n            45.3,\n            33.8,\n            \"8.1x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"pick_two\",\n            28.4,\n            48.3,\n            \"9.5x\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Per-task breakdown展示within-environment diversity并provide mechanistic validation：如果credit assignment decay是root cause，那longer tasks应该show greater episode-level advantage。r=0.61确认这个prediction。这也informs selective verification design：pick_two任务应receive more frequent verification because they're hardest and longest。\\n\\nTask difficulty与episode length高度相关(r=-0.72)。Examine最简单(62.5%)因为只需navigate+look——最短episodes(18.7步)。Pick_two最难(28.4%)因为需要两次independent object interactions——最长episodes(48.3步)。Episode-level advantage与task length正相关(r=0.61)：longer tasks受credit assignment问题影响更大，所以从episode-level training获益更多。Pick_two的episode-level improvement最dramatic(从~3% step-independent到28.4% episode-level，~9x)而examine improvement较modest(从~10%到62.5%，~6x)。这provides additional mechanistic evidence：episode-level training的benefit直接comes from solving longer-horizon credit assignment。\"\n  }\n]","numLines":944,"startLine":1,"totalLines":944}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XmfbH3QSm7B48CDNamYAh6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — Learning When to Verify: RL-Trained Selective Self-Verification for Interactive Agents\n2\t\n3\t> Post-MVP 重写 (2026-05-16) | 基于 D053 MVP 通过 + Reviewer 建议\n4\t\n5\t## Core Insight\n6\t\n7\tMulti-turn interactive agents 的 self-verification 大部分是 confirmatory（不改变行为）而非 corrective。但要训练 agent 学会 selective verification，首先需要解决一个被忽视的训练方法论问题：**step-independent RL 在长 horizon 任务中因 credit assignment decay (gamma^(T-h) → 0) 而灾难性崩溃**。Episode-level training 是前提条件。在此基础上，action-change 作为 intrinsic reward signal 训练 selective verification policy。\n8\t\n9\t## Story Arc\n10\t\n11\t**Dual contribution**: Training methodology + Selective verification system\n12\t\n13\t叙事线：\n14\t1. Self-verification 对 interactive agents 有用，但 always-on 成本高\n15\t2. 训练 agent 学 WHEN to verify 是自然方向 → 但现有 step-independent RL 框架在多轮任务上失败\n16\t3. 我们发现根因是 credit assignment decay，提出 episode-level GRPO 解决\n17\t4. 在此基础上，用 action-change 作为 verification informativeness 的 reward，训练 selective policy\n18\t5. 结果：near-always-on performance + 显著降低 verification cost\n19\t\n20\t## Target Venue\n21\t\n22\t待定（NeurIPS 2026 / EMNLP 2026 / ICLR 2026），取决于实验进度和最终效果。\n23\t\n24\t## Core Claims\n25\t\n26\t### Claim 1 (strength: strong): Episode-level credit assignment is critical for RL training of multi-turn agents\n27\t- 所需证据：episode-level vs step-independent 对比，不同 h 值的 ablation，mechanistic 分析\n28\t- 当前证据状态：**ESTABLISHED** (exp029 step5 val=25% vs exp028c step10 val=0%)\n29\t- 强度依据：2x baseline vs catastrophic collapse，机制清晰（gamma^49=7.7%）\n30\t\n31\t### Claim 2 (strength: moderate): Action-change is an effective intrinsic reward for verification informativeness\n32\t- 所需证据：selective verification 训练收敛 + action-change vs random/confidence baselines\n33\t- 当前证据状态：**not yet established**，依赖 Phase B 实验\n34\t- 前提：episode-level 训练的 agent 需达到 ≥40% success 才有意义\n35\t\n36\t### Claim 3 (strength: moderate): Learned selective policy matches always-on performance at reduced verification cost\n37\t- 所需证据：B-IAVR verification ↓40%+ 且 success delta < 3pp vs always-on\n38\t- 当前证据状态：**not yet established**，依赖 Phase B + C\n39\t- 前提：Claim 1 的 agent 需足够强\n40\t\n41\t## Contingency Plan\n42\t\n43\t如果 episode-level 训练收敛后 success 仍 < 40%（不足以支撑 cost-efficiency story）：\n44\t- **Plan A**（首选）：paper 变为 pure training methodology contribution — \"Episode-Level RL for Multi-Turn Agents: Why Step-Independent Fails and How to Fix It\"\n45\t- **Plan B**：加更多 ablation 深挖 episode-level training（context window size sweep, reward shaping, curriculum），做 analysis paper\n46\t- 不考虑 downgrade venue\n47\t\n48\t## Reviewer Attack Surface + Defense\n49\t\n50\t| # | Concern | Severity | Defense Experiment |\n51\t|---|---------|----------|--------------------|\n52\t| 1 | \"Episode-level RL is obvious / well-known\" | HIGH | Context window ablation (h=2,5,10,20,full) 展示 non-trivial threshold + 机制分析 + 展示现有 LLM-agent 工作(RAGEN等)默认 step-independent |\n53\t| 2 | Single environment (ALFWorld) | MEDIUM | 加 ScienceWorld / WebShop (if resources permit) |\n54\t| 3 | Small model (1.7B) | MEDIUM | 定位 resource-constrained; 加 7B 验证 (if GPU available) |\n55\t| 4 | Action-change = noise vs signal | MEDIUM | Entropy-controlled analysis + causal intervention (Phase B) |\n56\t| 5 | Selective verification 效果不够 significant | MEDIUM | 多 baseline 对比 (always-on / no-verify / random-p / confidence-threshold / ARES) |\n57\t| 6 | 与 ARES 差异化不足 | LOW | 实验直接对比 + 方法论差异表 (SFT router vs RL policy, continuous vs binary) |\n58\t\n59\t## Evidence Status Matrix\n60\t\n61\t| Claim | MVP Evidence | Research Evidence Needed | Priority |\n62\t|-------|-------------|--------------------------|----------|\n63\t| Claim 1 | exp029 vs exp028c (25% vs 0%) | h-value ablation, multi-seed, mechanism paper figure | P0 |\n64\t| Claim 2 | N/A | Phase B full implementation | P1 |\n65\t| Claim 3 | N/A | Phase B + C comparison suite | P1 |\n66\t\n67\t## Competitive Positioning\n68\t\n69\t| System | Method | ALFWorld | Key Difference |\n70\t|--------|--------|----------|---------------|\n71\t| Self-Guide (2026) | Always-on verification | 72.7% (1.7B) | We add selectivity via RL |\n72\t| ARES (2603.07915) | SFT router, continuous effort | 52.7% token↓ | SFT vs RL, continuous vs binary |\n73\t| Thinkless (NeurIPS'25) | RL control token | reasoning | Same RL philosophy, different domain |\n74\t| ReflAct (EMNLP'25) | Prompting GPT-4 | 93.3% | Different scale/approach |\n75\t| RAGEN (2025) | GRPO for agents | varies | Step-independent default — our baseline |\n76\t\n77\t## Research Phases\n78\t\n79\t1. **Phase A (DONE)**: Episode-level GRPO training — MVP passed, demonstrates Claim 1\n80\t2. **Phase A+**: Continue training to convergence (target ≥40% success), deploy tatsu parallel patch, multi-seed\n81\t3. **Phase B**: Implement selective verification with action-change reward — Claim 2 & 3\n82\t4. **Phase C**: Ablation suite — context window sweep, reward ablations, baseline comparisons\n83\t5. **Phase D**: (Conditional on resources) Multi-env / multi-model scaling\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad4aa9d2-b010-4eaf-be63-477490747ad9","uuid":"2846e6f0-fcfc-43a8-9805-6a8be427d0e2","timestamp":"2026-05-17T00:06:21.193Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_1/projects/cost-verify-agent-rl/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T235255/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — Learning When to Verify: RL-Trained Selective Self-Verification for Interactive Agents\n\n> Post-MVP 重写 (2026-05-16) | 基于 D053 MVP 通过 + Reviewer 建议\n\n## Core Insight\n\nMulti-turn interactive agents 的 self-verification 大部分是 confirmatory（不改变行为）而非 corrective。但要训练 agent 学会 selective verification，首先需要解决一个被忽视的训练方法论问题：**step-independent RL 在长 horizon 任务中因 credit assignment decay (gamma^(T-h) → 0) 而灾难性崩溃**。Episode-level training 是前提条件。在此基础上，action-change 作为 intrinsic reward signal 训练 selective verification policy。\n\n## Story Arc\n\n**Dual contribution**: Training methodology + Selective verification system\n\n叙事线：\n1. Self-verification 对 interactive agents 有用，但 always-on 成本高\n2. 训练 agent 学 WHEN to verify 是自然方向 → 但现有 step-independent RL 框架在多轮任务上失败\n3. 我们发现根因是 credit assignment decay，提出 episode-level GRPO 解决\n4. 在此基础上，用 action-change 作为 verification informativeness 的 reward，训练 selective policy\n5. 结果：near-always-on performance + 显著降低 verification cost\n\n## Target Venue\n\n待定（NeurIPS 2026 / EMNLP 2026 / ICLR 2026），取决于实验进度和最终效果。\n\n## Core Claims\n\n### Claim 1 (strength: strong): Episode-level credit assignment is critical for RL training of multi-turn agents\n- 所需证据：episode-level vs step-independent 对比，不同 h 值的 ablation，mechanistic 分析\n- 当前证据状态：**ESTABLISHED** (exp029 step5 val=25% vs exp028c step10 val=0%)\n- 强度依据：2x baseline vs catastrophic collapse，机制清晰（gamma^49=7.7%）\n\n### Claim 2 (strength: moderate): Action-change is an effective intrinsic reward for verification informativeness\n- 所需证据：selective verification 训练收敛 + action-change vs random/confidence baselines\n- 当前证据状态：**not yet established**，依赖 Phase B 实验\n- 前提：episode-level 训练的 agent 需达到 ≥40% success 才有意义\n\n### Claim 3 (strength: moderate): Learned selective policy matches always-on performance at reduced verification cost\n- 所需证据：B-IAVR verification ↓40%+ 且 success delta < 3pp vs always-on\n- 当前证据状态：**not yet established**，依赖 Phase B + C\n- 前提：Claim 1 的 agent 需足够强\n\n## Contingency Plan\n\n如果 episode-level 训练收敛后 success 仍 < 40%（不足以支撑 cost-efficiency story）：\n- **Plan A**（首选）：paper 变为 pure training methodology contribution — \"Episode-Level RL for Multi-Turn Agents: Why Step-Independent Fails and How to Fix It\"\n- **Plan B**：加更多 ablation 深挖 episode-level training（context window size sweep, reward shaping, curriculum），做 analysis paper\n- 不考虑 downgrade venue\n\n## Reviewer Attack Surface + Defense\n\n| # | Concern | Severity | Defense Experiment |\n|---|---------|----------|--------------------|\n| 1 | \"Episode-level RL is obvious / well-known\" | HIGH | Context window ablation (h=2,5,10,20,full) 展示 non-trivial threshold + 机制分析 + 展示现有 LLM-agent 工作(RAGEN等)默认 step-independent |\n| 2 | Single environment (ALFWorld) | MEDIUM | 加 ScienceWorld / WebShop (if resources permit) |\n| 3 | Small model (1.7B) | MEDIUM | 定位 resource-constrained; 加 7B 验证 (if GPU available) |\n| 4 | Action-change = noise vs signal | MEDIUM | Entropy-controlled analysis + causal intervention (Phase B) |\n| 5 | Selective verification 效果不够 significant | MEDIUM | 多 baseline 对比 (always-on / no-verify / random-p / confidence-threshold / ARES) |\n| 6 | 与 ARES 差异化不足 | LOW | 实验直接对比 + 方法论差异表 (SFT router vs RL policy, continuous vs binary) |\n\n## Evidence Status Matrix\n\n| Claim | MVP Evidence | Research Evidence Needed | Priority |\n|-------|-------------|--------------------------|----------|\n| Claim 1 | exp029 vs exp028c (25% vs 0%) | h-value ablation, multi-seed, mechanism paper figure | P0 |\n| Claim 2 | N/A | Phase B full implementation | P1 |\n| Claim 3 | N/A | Phase B + C comparison suite | P1 |\n\n## Competitive Positioning\n\n| System | Method | ALFWorld | Key Difference |\n|--------|--------|----------|---------------|\n| Self-Guide (2026) | Always-on verification | 72.7% (1.7B) | We add selectivity via RL |\n| ARES (2603.07915) | SFT router, continuous effort | 52.7% token↓ | SFT vs RL, continuous vs binary |\n| Thinkless (NeurIPS'25) | RL control token | reasoning | Same RL philosophy, different domain |\n| ReflAct (EMNLP'25) | Prompting GPT-4 | 93.3% | Different scale/approach |\n| RAGEN (2025) | GRPO for agents | varies | Step-independent default — our baseline |\n\n## Research Phases\n\n1. **Phase A (DONE)**: Episode-level GRPO training — MVP passed, demonstrates Claim 1\n2. **Phase A+**: Continue training to convergence (target ≥40% success), deploy tatsu parallel patch, multi-seed\n3. **Phase B**: Implement selective verification with action-change reward — Claim 2 & 3\n4. **Phase C**: Ablation suite — context window sweep, reward ablations, baseline comparisons\n5. **Phase D**: (Conditional on resources) Multi-env / multi-model scaling\n","numLines":84,"startLine":1,"totalLines":84}}}
